<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for the Swift app binary. Deliberately minimal: this file must
  NOT gain disable-library-validation. That relaxation belongs only on the
  bundled interpreter (see python-entitlements.plist); the app links nothing
  outside /System and /usr/lib and keeps library validation fully enforced.

  No apple-events. It was here from 2026-08-13 on the belief that reconnecting
  the NAS drove the Finder; it doesn't. The reconnect is a bare `mount volume`
  (BackupEngine.mountScriptArguments), which sends no Apple Event, so Kept
  never needs Automation. Verified 2026-10-13: a build without this
  entitlement reconnected an ejected share in under a second.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
</dict>
</plist>
